Reporting to the Senior Manager, Employee Communications, the Advisor is responsible for leading internal communication initiatives at the Mint. This role directly supports cultivating a positive and healthy workplace culture, articulating business goals to support employees in their day-to-day work, elevating the sense of community, supporting engagement and enablement through open communication, and ensuring employees have the information and context they need to excel.
Your Responsibilities:
- Develop content in support of the employee communications content plan and strategy in collaboration with the leadership team;
- Support content development for various reports, including legislative reports
- Publish digital and print publications;
- Collaborate with public affairs to align key corporate messaging;
- Develop and support delivery of corporate communication internal content;
- Lead communication activities in support of corporate initiatives, meetings, and events, including managing vendors, budgeting and on-site execution of these key initiatives.
